Theorem RL-11a: dynamic reuse for MaybeShared — IsShared check; unique fast / shared slow

  Preconditions:
    - RL-11a governs dynamic reuse per Annex E §AIMS Allocation Reuse:
      "Dynamic reuse for MaybeShared: emit IsShared check; unique ->
      Reset/Reuse fast path, shared -> fresh allocation slow path. Requires
      DP-6 eligibility."
    - Signature ArcFunction x AimsStateMap -> ArcFunction per
      the canonical proof notation:264; discharged against the sec-01
      Realization.proof sorry obligation.
    - DP-6 (is_reuse_candidate) admits MaybeShared as a CANDIDATE (Owned,
      not Shared, reusable shape); RL-11 requires static Unique, so a
      MaybeShared candidate uses the runtime IsShared branch instead.
    - Shipped: emit_reuse/dynamic.rs (the IsShared branch);
      emit_reuse/detect.rs (DP-6 candidate detection).
    - depends-on sec-05: DP-6 (is_reuse_candidate) soundness.

  Soundness property:
    Forall MaybeShared owned reusable value v:

      (P1) Branch decision: RL-11a emits a runtime IsShared check; the unique
           runtime branch (RC == 1) takes the Reset/Reuse fast path; the
           shared runtime branch (RC > 1) takes the fresh-allocation slow
           path.

      (P2) Value-semantics preservation: reuse fires ONLY on the unique
           runtime branch (v is the sole owner, no alias observes the reuse);
           the shared branch fresh-allocates, leaving every alias intact.
           Both branches preserve correctness.

    RL-11a refines plain ARC by reusing the dying allocation whenever the
    runtime proves sole ownership, falling back to a fresh allocation only
    when an alias actually exists.

  Proof obligation:
    Constructive discharge by the case_analysis engine.

    Part (P1/P2) — runtime-branch enumeration:
      The verifier asserts DP-6 eligibility for the MaybeShared value, then
      enumerates both runtime branches:
        runtime_unique = true -> reuse fast path fires (sound)
        runtime_unique = false -> fresh-allocation slow path (no reuse)
      Coverage gate: 2 runtime branches. Negative-direction witness: reuse
      MUST NOT fire on the shared (RC > 1) runtime branch (it would corrupt
      the alias) — asserted.

    Engines dispatched:
      case_analysis (PRIMARY — section_08::verify_rl11a_dynamic_reuse;
        DP-6 eligibility + runtime-branch enumeration; emits Fail on an
        unsound branch or a wrong fire)
      rc_counting (SECONDARY — gracious-accept per the coverage-manifest RL
        row)
      refinement (SECONDARY — gracious-accept per the coverage-manifest RL
        row)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: section_08 case_analysis engine discharges RL-11a via DP-6 eligibility for the MaybeShared value + runtime IsShared branch enumeration (unique RC==1 -> Reset/Reuse fast path; shared RC>1 -> fresh-allocation slow path) with a negative-direction witness rejecting reuse on the shared branch, grounded in the shipped emit_reuse/dynamic.rs IsShared realization
